What is Monodisperse Fluorescent Microsphere?
Monodisperse Fluorescent Microspheres are precision‑engineered polymer or composite particles that exhibit an exceptionally uniform size distribution while embedding stable fluorescent signals. Their consistent diameter, reliable fluorescence intensity and tunable surface chemistry make them indispensable for immunoassays, molecular diagnostics, flow cytometry, calibration standards and bio‑separation workflows. In 2025, global production reached roughly 500 tons at an average price of USD 780 000 per ton, with leading suppliers reporting gross margins ranging from 42 % to 65 %-a clear indication of the premium value attached to tight particle tolerances.
